  "interpretation": "<p>Hemoglobin A2 is a <strong data-start=\"107\" data-end=\"146\">minor component of adult hemoglobin</strong>, composed of two alpha and two delta chains. It normally makes up <strong data-start=\"220\" data-end=\"262\">a small percentage of total hemoglobin</strong> and is commonly measured to <strong data-start=\"291\" data-end=\"325\">screen for &beta; -thalassemia trait</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"701\" data-end=\"744\"><strong data-start=\"708\" data-end=\"744\">Elevated HbA₂ (&gt; 3.5%) &ndash; Causes:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"746\" data-end=\"880\">\n<li data-start=\"746\" data-end=\"801\"><strong data-start=\"748\" data-end=\"781\">&beta;-Thalassemia Trait (Carrier)</strong> &ndash; Most common cause</li>\n<li data-start=\"802\" data-end=\"858\"><strong data-start=\"804\" data-end=\"828\">Megaloblastic anemia</strong> (e.g., B12/folate deficiency)</li>\n<li data-start=\"859\" data-end=\"880\"><strong data-start=\"861\" data-end=\"880\">Hyperthyroidism</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"887\" data-end=\"925\"><strong data-start=\"894\" data-end=\"925\">Low HbA₂ (&lt; 2.0%) &ndash; Causes:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"927\" data-end=\"1026\">\n<li data-start=\"927\" data-end=\"955\"><strong data-start=\"929\" data-end=\"955\">Iron deficiency anemia</strong></li>\n<li data-start=\"956\" data-end=\"981\"><strong data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"981\">&alpha;-Thalassemia trait</strong></li>\n<li data-start=\"982\" data-end=\"1008\"><strong data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1001\">&delta;-thalassemia</strong> (rare)</li>\n<li data-start=\"1009\" data-end=\"1026\">Chronic illness</li>\n</ul>",
